NOTE ON THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL

The MIT grant above covers the code written by the copyright holder. It does
NOT and cannot grant rights over third-party material referenced by that code.

The scripts embed a small factual data excerpt (a 4 x 9 table of retention
times, 36 numeric values) taken from the supplementary material of:

    Zisi, Ch., Pappa-Louisi, A., & Nikitas, P. (2020). Separation optimization
    in HPLC analysis implemented in R programming language.
    Journal of Chromatography A, 1617, 460823.
    https://doi.org/10.1016/j.chroma.2019.460823

That excerpt is included with attribution as a de minimis quotation so the
published results can be reproduced for teaching. It represents roughly 0.014%
of the cells in the original supplementary workbook. Rights in the article and
its supplementary material remain with the original authors and publisher; they
are not redistributed here. If you reuse this code, keep the attribution and
cite the original paper — the retention models and the optimisation method are
their scientific contribution, not the copyright holder's.
